course: dictionary
lesson: 12673
title: Distinctive: easy to spot
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Distinctive means easy to recognise because it is different from others. Something distinctive is special to one person or thing. «The zebra has distinctive black and white stripes.» You can pick out a zebra from far away because of its stripes.
explain: When you meet distinctive, ask yourself: what makes this one different? The words around it give you the clue. «Dad has a distinctive whistle.» The whistle must be unlike anyone else's, or the sentence would not single it out.
explain: Scientists use distinctive features to tell living things apart. «A robin has a distinctive red breast.» That red patch helps you identify a robin quickly. Writers use distinctive voices and smells in the same way, so the reader knows which character is speaking.
fact: Distinctive means easy to recognise because it is different from others.
fact: «Distinctive features» are the special parts that help you identify a plant or animal.
fact: «A distinctive smell» is one you would know again straight away.
fact: Distinctive is an adjective: you can say more distinctive or most distinctive.
fact: A good check is to ask, "Is this different from the others in a way that makes it easy to spot?"
exercise: «The robin has a distinctive red breast.» What does distinctive mean here? | *Brown and dull | Easy to recognise because it is different | Very small | Hard to see at all
exercise: «Each singer in the choir has a distinctive voice.» Which meaning fits best? | The same as every other voice | *Special to that singer, so you know who is singing | Quiet and hard to hear | Very loud and sudden
exercise: Ella says, «Dad's distinctive whistle means he is home.» Why is the whistle distinctive? | It is written in a book | *It sounds like no one else's | It is the same as everyone's whistle | It is very quiet
test: Which phrase means the same as distinctive? | Very old | Wet and grey | Hard to notice | *Special and easy to spot
test: Which sentence uses distinctive correctly? | The tiger is distinctive because it is sleeping. | I had a distinctive lunch of cold toast. Hmm, that is wrong. | The distinctive river is sad. | *The tiger's orange coat with black stripes is distinctive.
exam: Why does a scientist look for distinctive features when identifying a plant? | *To tell it apart from other plants | To find out how old the plant is | To make the plant smell nicer | To make the plant hard to find
